{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "the social network is a masterfully crafted film that explores the birth of facebook and the complex relationships behind its creation. directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, the movie weaves together multiple timelines to tell the story of mark zuckerberg's rise from a college student to a tech mogul. the screenplay is sharp, witty, and dialog-driven, propelling the narrative forward with relentless energy. jesse eisenberg delivers a standout performance as zuckerberg, portraying him as brilliant yet socially awkward and emotionally distant. the supporting cast, including andrew garfield as eduardo saverin and jesse eisenberg's rival, provides strong counterpoints that highlight the themes of betrayal and ambition. trent reznor and atticus ross composed an atmospheric and haunting score that perfectly complements the film's cold and calculating tone. visually, fincher uses a cool color palette and precise framing to create a sense of detachment, mirroring the characters' isolation despite their digital connectivity. the film does not shy away from the moral ambiguities of the tech industry, questioning the cost of success and the nature of friendship in the modern age. it is a compelling drama that feels both timeless and urgently contemporary, cementing its place as one of the best films of the twenty-first century.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.00788493}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.00071145565}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.01125169}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " master", "logprob": -0.057332832}, {"token": "fully", "logprob": -0.695188}, {"token": " crafted", "logprob": -0.00026998587}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.25565588}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0033091162}, {"token": " explores", "logprob": -0.9541018}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0003